## MemoPayload: schema and role

`MemoPayload` is the persisted JSON blob on each memo row (`memo.payload`), defined in `proto/store/memo.proto`:

```7:28:proto/store/memo.proto
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;

  Location location = 2;

  repeated string tags = 3;

  // The calculated properties from the memo content.
  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    // The title extracted from the first H1 heading, if present.
    string title = 5;
  }

  message Location {
    string placeholder = 1;
    double latitude = 2;
    double longitude = 3;
  }
}
```

Only **`property`** and **`tags`** are content-derived. **`location`** is user-supplied via the API and merged separately (see triggers below).

---

## Where computation happens

### 1. Assembly entry point: `RebuildMemoPayload`

```74:87:server/runner/memopayload/runner.go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
	if memo.Payload == nil {
		memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
	}

	// Use goldmark service to extract all metadata in a single pass (more efficient)
	data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
	if err != nil {
		return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
	}

	memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
	memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
	return nil
}
```

This writes **`Tags`** and **`Property`** only; it does not touch **`Location`**.

### 2. Extraction engine: `markdown.Service.ExtractAll`

Configured with tag and mention extensions in `server/router/api/v1/v1.go:48-51`.

Core logic in `internal/markdown/markdown.go:355-421`:

| Field | Extraction rule | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| `tags` | Walk AST for `#tag` nodes (`mast.TagNode`), skip tags inside links/images; dedupe preserving case | 376-378, 417-418 |
| `property.title` | Plain text of the **first block-level child** of the document if it is an H1 heading | 383-388 |
| `property.has_link` | Any `Link` node | 392-394 |
| `property.has_code` | Any `CodeBlock`, `FencedCodeBlock`, or `CodeSpan` | 396-397 |
| `property.has_task_list` | Any GFM task checkbox (`TaskCheckBox`) | 399-400 |
| `property.has_incomplete_tasks` | Any **unchecked** task checkbox | 401-404 |

Lower-level helpers also exist (`ExtractTags` at `142-169`, `ExtractProperties` at `192-240`) but production rebuild uses **`ExtractAll`** only.

**Not stored in MemoPayload:** `ExtractAll` also collects `Mentions` (`379-381`), but `RebuildMemoPayload` ignores them. Mentions are used at notification time via `resolveMentionTargets` in `server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:32-35`.

---

## What triggers recomputation

### Create (including comments)

`CreateMemo` always rebuilds before persist:

```108:113:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, create, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
	}
	if request.Memo.Location != nil {
		create.Payload.Location = convertLocationToStore(request.Memo.Location)
	}
```

`CreateMemoComment` (`server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:56-59`) delegates to `CreateMemo`, so comments get the same rebuild.

### Update (content only)

Rebuild runs **only** when the update mask includes `"content"`:

```436:451:server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
		if path == "content" {
			contentUpdated = true
			previousContent = memo.Content
			// ...
			memo.Content = request.Memo.Content
			if err := memopayload.RebuildMemoPayload(ctx, memo, s.MarkdownService); err != nil {
				return nil, status.Errorf(codes.Internal, "failed to rebuild memo payload: %v", err)
			}
			update.Content = &memo.Content
			update.Payload = memo.Payload
```

Updating **`location`** alone (`481-484`) copies user location into existing payload without recomputing tags/properties. Other update paths (visibility, pinned, state, timestamps, attachments, relations) do **not** trigger rebuild.

### Batch runner / migration

`server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:26-72` defines `Runner.RunOnce`, which lists all memos in batches of 100, calls `RebuildMemoPayload`, and persists via `Store.UpdateMemo`.

**No production caller exists:** `memopayload.NewRunner` / `RunOnce` are not referenced from `server/server.go`, `cmd/`, or `scripts/`. The runner is a standalone batch rebuilder, not wired into server startup (unlike `s3presign` at `server/server.go:162-169`).

---

## How payload reaches lists/previews

Stored payload is mapped to the API `Memo` message in `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go:47-50`:

```47:50:server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go
	if memo.Payload != nil {
		memoMessage.Tags = memo.Payload.Tags
		memoMessage.Property = convertMemoPropertyFromStore(memo.Payload.Property)
		memoMessage.Location = convertLocationFromStore(memo.Payload.Location)
```

Property field mapping: `315-325:server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go`.

Payload fields power:
- **List filtering** — CEL/filter schema reads `memo.payload` JSON paths (`internal/filter/schema.go:173-228`): `tags`, `has_task_list`, `has_link`, `has_code`, `has_incomplete_tasks`
- **Frontend filters** — `property.hasLink`, `property.hasTaskList`, `property.hasCode` (`web/src/contexts/MemoFilterContext.tsx:11-13`)
- **User stats** — incomplete-task counts from `memo.Payload.Property.HasIncompleteTasks` (`server/router/api/v1/user_service_stats.go:151,267`)

Persisted as protojson in DB: e.g. `store/db/postgres/memo.go:17-26` (create), `226-230` (update).

