## Snippet vs MemoPayload (distinct)

**Snippet is not part of MemoPayload.** It is computed on-the-fly at API response time from raw content:

```76:80:server/router/api/v1/memo_service_converter.go
	snippet, err := s.getMemoContentSnippet(memo.Content)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, errors.Wrap(err, "failed to get memo content snippet")
	}
	memoMessage.Snippet = snippet
```

Implementation: `getMemoContentSnippet` → `MarkdownService.GenerateSnippet(content, 64)` at `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:83-89`.

`GenerateSnippet` (`internal/markdown/markdown.go:263-345`) walks the AST, extracts plain text (skips fenced/code blocks, includes inline code/tags), truncates at word boundary to max length. **Not persisted**; recomputed on every memo read/conversion.

Snippet is also generated for relations (`memo_service_converter.go:224-229`), relation API (`memo_relation_service.go:154,162`), and notifications (`user_service_notifications.go:323-327`).

Used in UI for previews: e.g. `web/src/components/MemoView/components/MemoCommentListView.tsx:45`, `UserMemoMap.tsx:154`, relation cards.

